## REST Client keeps cookies between requests, so the refresh_token cookie
## from login is sent to /auth/refresh and /auth/logout automatically.
## Seeded users: alice, bob, carol, dave, erin / password123

## Sign up - expect 201 { accessToken, user } + refresh_token cookie
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "makarena",
    "email": "johndoe@example.com",
    "password": "Veryoriginal1!"
}

###
## Log in - expect 200 { accessToken, user } + refresh_token cookie
# @name login
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "login": "alice",
    "password": "password123"
}

###
## Who am I - expect 200 (uses the access token from "login" above)
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

###
## Who am I without a token - expect 401 "Missing access token"
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/me

###
## Garbage token - expect 401 "Invalid or expired access token"
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer abc

###
## Create a post as the logged-in user - expect 201, authorId = alice
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "body": "Posted with a token"
}

###
## Refresh - expect 200 { accessToken } + a NEW refresh_token cookie
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/refresh

###
## Log out - expect 204, cookie cleared
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/logout

###
## Refresh after logout - expect 401 (no cookie anymore)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/refresh

###
## Wrong password - expect 401 "Invalid login or password"
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "login": "alice",
    "password": "Wrongpassword1!"
}

###
## Unknown login - expect 401 with the same message
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "login": "nobodyatall",
    "password": "Veryoriginal1!"
}

###
## Username containing @ on signup - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "john@example.com",
    "email": "other@example.com",
    "password": "Veryoriginal1!"
}
